{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>If ransom is imposed upon him.</b> That the heirs want to accept ransom for the killing of their father." "<b>According to all that is imposed upon him.</b> Since it [the ox] did not kill by direct act of a court, the court is permitted to impose ransom upon him, since the heirs are willing to accept it." "<b>If ransom.</b> It is not one of the counted obligations, as explained regarding ואם מזבח אבנים."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:31.911975676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}